course: dictionary
lesson: 7991
title: Rectangular shapes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rectangular means shaped like a rectangle, with four straight sides and square corners. Think of a door, a book cover or a sheet of paper. «In the UK, circular road signs give orders, triangular signs warn and rectangular signs give information.» The shape of each sign tells you its job.
explain: A rectangular box or room is a cuboid, also called a rectangular prism, with rectangle faces. When a text talks about a length and a width, as in «a rectangular pool», it is describing a shape you could measure. Look for clues like size, flat surfaces or words about measuring.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Goats have wide rectangular pupils» makes sense if rectangular means the shape of a rectangle. It would not make sense if it meant a colour or a feeling, so the clue points to shape.
fact: Rectangular means shaped like a rectangle, with four straight sides and square corners.
fact: «Rectangular» is an adjective, so it describes things such as a field, a garden, a room, a box or a pool.
fact: A rectangular box is also called a cuboid, or a rectangular prism.
fact: In the UK, «rectangular signs give information», while circular signs give orders and triangular signs warn.
fact: «Goats have wide rectangular pupils» that help them see almost all the way round.
exercise: «In the UK, triangular signs warn and rectangular signs give information.» What shape is a rectangular sign? | Three sides and three corners | *Four straight sides with square corners | Oval with curved edges | Round with no corners
exercise: A maths student says a garden with a length and a width is rectangular. What does rectangular mean here? | Covered with grass | Shaped like a circle | Very long and thin like a snake | *Shaped like a rectangle, with four straight sides and square corners
exercise: Which of these is a rectangular prism? | A ball | *A shoebox | A coin | A cone
test: «The envelope was rectangular, with square corners.» What shape is the envelope? | Star | Triangle | Circle | *Rectangle
test: Why is a rectangular room described as rectangular? | It has a round window | It is painted white | *Its shape has four straight sides and square corners | It is very old
exam: «Rectangular» means which of these? | Pointed like a star | Shiny and smooth | Round like a ball | *Shaped like a rectangle, with four straight sides and square corners
